    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Week in Dublin",
          "heading": "Jake White's Fiji trained at Salmo before losing 15-43 to Ireland",
          "body": "Dublin junior club De La Salle Palmerston FC, known locally as Salmo, hosted the squad all week, and its director of rugby, Norman Byrne, called the players \"the nicest people you’ll ever come across.\" Fiji moved their captain's run to Kirwan Park rather than the Aviva Stadium, and forwards coach Gert Smal watched on as Josua Tuisova and Jiuta Wainiqolo were on the pitch. They then lost 15-43 to Ireland at the Aviva Stadium on Saturday night."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "Italy lose 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's missed touch-kick. France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Aviva Stadium, Dublin"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "The42"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Record haul",
          "heading": "Will Joseph scores five tries to equal England's Test record",
          "body": "Will Joseph's hat-trick came inside 20 minutes of Saturday's 78-15 win over Japan, and a fifth try after the break left him level with Douglas Lambert, Rory Underwood, Josh Lewsey and Henry Arundell as the only England men to score five in a Test. Joseph, 24, won his only previous cap under Eddie Jones in 2022. With Immanuel Feyi-Waboso out for the rest of the tournament, former England wing Chris Ashton told BBC Radio 5 Live that Joseph is \"pretty similar\" to Feyi-Waboso in how he plays."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Italy lose 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's missed touch-kick",
          "body": "France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship; Matthieu Jalibert nears return",
          "body": "Hooker Julien Marchand, who felt further tightness in his thigh during the warm-up against South Africa, is ruled out for the rest of the competition, Planet Rugby has confirmed. Peato Mauvaka started in his place, after Marchand had already missed the start of the French camp with a hamstring injury, and Guillaume Cramont becomes France's reserve hooker. Matthieu Jalibert, out since a quadriceps injury in September, is expected at Marcoussis early next week, news Fabien Galthié will welcome given his fly-half options have been decimated by injury."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "Italy lose 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's missed touch-kick. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Stade de France, Saint-Denis",
        "referee": "Hollie Davidson"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match review",
          "heading": "Andy Farrell admitted Ireland made too many errors in beating Fiji",
          "body": "Fiji's quick tries from Josua Tuisova and Peceli Yato overturned Tommy O'Brien's early opener, and Ireland trailed briefly before leading 17-15 at the break. They pulled clear in the second half for a 43-15 win, but Farrell was blunt about the start. \"There were too many errors from us and we were losing ground, certainly in the first half physically,\" he told Virgin Media Sport. The result leaves Ireland level on 20 points with England, a point behind France, ahead of South Africa next week."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "Italy lose 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's missed touch-kick. France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ]
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Genoa defeat",
          "heading": "Garbisi's missed touch-kick sinks Italy as Argentina edge Genoa 19-14",
          "body": "Italy led early through Monty Ioane's corner try, but Saturday's match at the Stadio Luigi Ferraris turned on Argentina's second-half tries. Rodrigo Isgró and Mateo Carreras crossed for Argentina, and Italy were awarded a penalty try after Efraín Elías was shown a yellow card for bringing down a maul. Italy pressed against 14 men but kept undermining their attacks with mistakes, and the final act was Paolo Garbisi's missed penalty touch-kick while trying to set up a lineout in a scoring position."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Stadio Luigi Ferraris, Genoa"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Americas Rugby News"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Matchday honour",
          "heading": "Joey Sharp, who overcame a brain tumour, to deliver Murrayfield match ball",
          "body": "Joey Sharp, who is five, will deliver the match ball alongside Commonwealth Games swimmer Archie Goodburn, and Scottish Rugby have arranged for him and his mother, Sam Sharp, to meet the players. It will be his first visit to Murrayfield, and accessible seating has been arranged for the family. Joey was diagnosed with a brain tumour at 11 days old, underwent three surgeries and nine rounds of chemotherapy, and now lives with cerebral palsy and visual impairments. Goodburn lives with three brain tumours himself."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "Italy lose 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's missed touch-kick. France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Murrayfield, Edinburgh"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Daily Record"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Emotional scenes",
          "heading": "Alex Cuthbert overwhelmed in BBC commentary box as Wales beat All Blacks",
          "body": "Former Wales wing Alex Cuthbert could barely speak when the final whistle sounded in Cardiff, and footage from the BBC Radio 5 Live commentary box shows him struggling to contain himself as the Principality Stadium erupted. \"Oh my God, I don't know what to say. Wow, what?! Just unbelievable,\" he said. He singled out the second half, saying \"The heart those boys showed, you could see it\". The win ended 34 straight defeats to the All Blacks, a run stretching back to 1953."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "Italy lose 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's missed touch-kick. France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury cover",
          "heading": "Bautista Bernasconi starts at hooker and scores as Pumas injuries pile up",
          "body": "Benetton hooker Bautista Bernasconi started against Italy after injuries to Julián Montoya, Ignacio Ruiz and Leonel Oviedo, and he made the most of the chance, driving over from a maul just before half-time to put the Pumas level at 7-7. The absences go further, with Thomas Gallo, Santiago Grondona, Marcos Kremer and Joaquín Oviedo also injured. Argentina still won 19-14, with Bernasconi's afternoon offering reassurance about the depth behind the first choice."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon at flyhalf after broken leg."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Americas Rugby News"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Carter Gordon recalled at flyhalf as Les Kiss restores Rob Valetini",
          "body": "Les Kiss has restored Carter Gordon to the No 10 jersey for Sunday's Scotland test, the playmaker back from a broken leg, the latest of several injuries to derail his progress. Rob Valetini returns to six alongside Harry Wilson and Fraser McReight, while Declan Meredith, who looked lost against England, is dropped from the match-day 23. Seven different flyhalves have started since the last World Cup. \"Carter will bring his flavour, he will bring his voice,\" Kiss said, with the Wallabies staring at a fourth straight Test defeat."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England thrash Japan 78-15 as Joseph equals Test try record",
          "body": "Italy lose 19-14 to Argentina after Garbisi's missed touch-kick. France hooker Julien Marchand ruled out of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
